  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-2\\le 2x-6\\le 4$ or $12x-22<14?$",
  "worked_solution": "We start by solving $-2\\le 2x-6\\le 4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\le 2x-6\\le 4 \\\\ 4 & \\le 2x\\le 10 \\\\ 2 & \\le x\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/c82330c4ccd9aff01ac73cd1ebac56d50f685e0da258fb83ec619ebd11023694.png)\n\nThen, we solve $12x-22<14:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-22 & <14 \\\\ 12x & <36 \\\\ x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/8ade78ec1b4adac7ee63d1eb3e5b5cc82ffe5b00437add005b7824dc2e0c05a9.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252742/assets/72edfbf24542f84652d24d879c2298cff603f960a22885e0b8856635a80d201c.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 5.$",
